# One-off data fix (August 2026): restore correct track ordering on 36 shows
# where tracks (sandwich songs, banter, cut/continued partials) were appended
# to the end of the show with wrong positions. Desired orders derived from
# phish.net setlists cross-checked against track ID adjacency (tracks were
# originally imported in setlist order, so a misplaced track's ID sits between
# the IDs of its correct neighbors).
#
# Run: bin/rails tracks:fix_positions
#
# Each show is verified by ID set before touching it and skipped with a
# warning if its tracks don't match expectations. Already-correct shows are
# no-ops, so the task is idempotent. Soundcheck tracks are placed first,
# consistent with the pre-show/soundcheck reorder; running the two in either
# order converges.
#
# By default only the 29 confirmed shows are applied. The 7 shows below
# contain placement judgment calls and are deferred unless INCLUDE_REVIEW=true:
#   1988-06-19  (cut)/(continued) pairs placed contiguously; verify by listening
#   1989-03-03  Banter x2 placed at end of Set 1 (exact spot unknown)
#   1991-03-17  Banter x3 end of Set 2, Banter x1 end of Encore (exact spots unknown)
#   1991-10-24  Banter placed at end of Set 1 (exact spot unknown)
#   1992-04-21  Noodling placed at end of Set 1 / end of Set 2 (exact spots unknown)
#   1992-05-12  Banter placed at end of Set 2 (exact spot unknown)
#   1993-08-15  Narration placed between Forbin's Ascent and Mockingbird (standard Gamehendge spot)
#
# This task can be deleted once it has been run in production.
